--title=iv-provision
# This list controls INCLUSION only, not order: verified 2026-09-15 by rendering
# the site, the generated nav is sorted ALPHABETICALLY BY FILENAME regardless of
# the order here (bootstrap, building, consuming, design, registry, releases,
# retiring, tailnet). Reading order is therefore expressed in index.qmd's
# "Where to go next" table instead. Numeric filename prefixes would force the
# sidebar order but would change every page URL and break inbound links, which
# is not worth it for a nine-page site that has a landing page.
#
# Restructured 2026-09-15: index.qmd was carrying the design rationale AND the
# full release history, which is why the site had no landing page and the host's
# non-provisioning roles were invisible.
--include=index.qmd
--include=design.md
--include=bootstrap.md
--include=building.md
--include=consuming.md
--include=tailnet.md
--include=registry.md
# retiring.md existed in the repo but was never on the site, while dotfiles docs
# cite it as the runbook for the one unrecoverable fleet operation. That looked
# like an oversight rather than intent.
--include=retiring.md
--include=releases.md
